  "_harness": "__alloca_probe cannot run here: a stub leaves ESP at EBP (the 0x1024-byte frame then overlaps the call stack) and a passthrough never returns (ESP ends lower). So strcpy/strlen/sprintf are scripted: nothing reads the overlapped stack except through them. With ESP = EBP, timeText (EBP-0x24) holds strlen's return address in [0..3] and the earlier pushed args above; strlen's scripted length picks the byte tested for '\\n': len 0x31 -> EBP+0x0C (low byte of the first vararg, a1), len 0x21 -> EBP-0x04 (now = time()).",
